{"availability":"available","full":"rolandkrueger/git-whiteboard-app","name":"git-whiteboard-app","description":"Web app to visualize Git functionality in a Git history graph for training purposes","category":"Design","language":"Kotlin","stars":21,"forks":2,"created":"2020-04-30T15:12:10Z","updated":"2026-08-28T14:28:22Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://git-whiteboard.netlify.app/","topics":["git","kotlin","teaching","teaching-assistant","webapp","whiteboard"],"demo":"https://git-whiteboard.netlify.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:02:09.324Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:02:09.324Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:02:09.324Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:02:09.324Z","stars":21,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Git Whiteboard App is a stateless (i.e. purely client-side) web application that allows you to quickly and easily create Git graphs in your browser for demonstration purposes. The application is designed to provide all the visual possibilities that are usually required on a whiteboard to draw Git graphs: Commit graphs, HEAD, branch and tag labels, simplified commit IDs, commits which are lost in the reflog, etc. The handling must be quick and easy, so that during a Git training course, for example, you can create a simple demo Git graph with a few mouse clicks to explain a specific Git…","This is the app in action. It shows a simple demo Git history which can be used to explain and demonstrate a number of Git features:","With the current version, you can demonstrate the following Git features:"],"features":["amend the HEAD commit,","cherry-pick commits,","add branches and tags,","delete branches and tags,","create a detached HEAD and create commits in detached HEAD state,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rolandkrueger/git-whiteboard-app/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"170dfb48dfd65cb265260c954145fa448c83d2a1dea80627fc0da8c48